      "properties": {
        "id": "housing_peristyle_house",
        "typology": "peristyle_house",
        "name": "Peristyle houses",
        "regions": "Hellenistic East (Greece, Aegean, western Anatolia, Levant), Baetica (southern Spain)",
        "notes": "A Greek-derived house plan wrapping rooms around a colonnaded courtyard rather than a Roman atrium, standard across the Aegean and the Levant since Hellenistic times. Delos's House of Dionysus, built in the 2nd century BCE, arranged its rooms around a mosaic-paved peristyle with a marble fountain. The same plan reached Roman Baetica, seen in the excavated peristyle villa at Salar near Granada.",
        "sources": [
          "https://greekreporter.com/2026/02/06/house-dionysus-delos-golden-age-ancient-greece/",
          "https://www.andaluciamia.com/en/tourism-on-archaeological-site-andalucia-villa-of-salar/",
          "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peristyle"
        ]
      }
    },
