      "properties": {
        "id": "housing_trullo_mudbrick",
        "typology": "trullo_mudbrick",
        "name": "Trulli and mudbrick vaulted dwellings",
        "regions": "Apulia (southern Italy), North Africa interior",
        "notes": "Dry-stone corbelling raised a conical roof without mortar or timber, a technique already used in Bronze Age tholos tombs and kept alive on Apulia's Murge plateau for field shelters and storehouses. Roman-era farms in the semi-arid North African interior built a parallel vaulted tradition in mudbrick and stone; survey work along Tripolitania's Wadi Sofeggin recorded barrel-vaulted farm buildings on the pre-desert frontier Trajan's forces were then pushing into.",
        "sources": [
          "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trullo",
          "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/269507991_Farming_the_Desert_The_UNESCO_Libyan_Valleys_Archaeological_Survey",
          "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gasr_Banat"
        ]
      }
    },
